  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Vaugrenier beach is at the western end of Villeneuve-Loubet, on the Antibes side: a natural beach with a water-sports base on site and access via the cycle path.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The Villeneuve-Loubet tourist office states that it is the only beach in the town that accepts animals, and that it is open daily, closed from midnight to 6am. Barbecues are banned. The office doesn't detail the leash rule; a Cannes tourist office document (2023) says "animals kept on a leash", which remains the cautious choice. We found no official source confirming a dog shower or a specific type of ground.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: the nearby Vaugrenier departmental park offers a 4.8 km forest circuit where dogs on a leash are allowed, according to the tourist office.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The Hippodrome beach in Cagnes-sur-Mer, where an area is reserved for dogs, is a few minutes away by car.</p>
    </div>

